      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Readington_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first German Lutheran Church in New Jersey was built in Readington in 1729‑30 on land donated by a free black man, Aray Van Guinee.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.readington.gov/visitor/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Taylor's Mill, a 1760 brick gristmill, sits on the National Register of Historic Places and once powered local farmers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Readington_Township%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Readington Village, the township’s oldest settled community, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places and dates back to the 1700s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.readington.gov/visitor/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Norfolk Southern Railway’s Lehigh Line, formerly the mainline of the Lehigh Valley Railroad, still runs through Readington, echoing its 19th‑century rail heritage.",
